nel bucket entirely).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`_repair_run` flags ANY ticket with a non-empty bucket: `if plan[\"retire\"] or plan[\"auto_orphans\"] or plan[\"triage_orphans\"]` (fsck_repair.py:290)","`_repair_ticket` triggers a rebuild when `plan[\"auto_orphans\"]` is present (fsck_repair.py:222); stale-channel is NOT currently a `_repair_plan` bucket — it lives only in `_check_snapshot`/`_scan` (fsck.py:289-298)","`--only` is not wired anywhere in `_commands` (search for `only=` returned only an unrelated hit), so the selector-vs-default gating is a genuinely new, unspecified decision","Plan step 3: 'Add SNAPSHOT_STALE_CHANNEL detection as a new bucket in _repair_plan, then expose a narrow ... selector through _repair_run'; step 4 + AC: 'Preserve existing rebar fsck --repair behavior when --only is absent'"],"finding":"The plan adds SNAPSHOT_STALE_CHANNEL as a new bucket in the SHARED `_repair_plan` (consumed by both default `--repair` and the new `--only=stale-channel` selector) but does not specify the gating mechanism that keeps the new bucket OUT of the default (no-`--only`) flag/rebuild trigger; without this pinned, the implementer either breaks the 'default `--repair` unchanged' contract (rebuilding ~550 stale-channel tickets in the plain path) or leaves `--only=stale-channel` a no-op.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f537dbd85e8c8cacd","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Pre-window preparation steps 3-4; AC 'Existing unfiltered fsck --repair behavior is unchanged' and 'fsck --repair --only=stale-channel selects only stale-channel snapshots'","norm_id":"n385c98323b432561","priority":0.4765,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An operator runs plain `rebar fsck --repair` (no `--only`) after this lands: if the new stale-channel bucket feeds the default flag/rebuild trigger, ~550 stale-channel tickets are rebuilt in that path, contradicting the unchanged-behavior AC and defeating the 550-vs-10 blast-radius isolation the narrow mode exists to provide.","Conversely, if the bucket is defined but never wired to a rebuild trigger, `--only=stale-channel` performs no repair and the quiet-window zero-stale-channel criterion cannot be met."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that `_repair_plan` always populates the new `stale_channel` bucket, but `_repair_run`/`_repair_ticket` accept an `only` selector: the default (no `--only`) path keeps its current inclusion/rebuild predicates (retire/auto_orphans) and never acts on `stale_channel`, while `--only=stale-channel` restricts inclusion AND the rebuild trigger to the `stale_channel` bucket (and applies the mixed-fault refusal when retire/orphan buckets are also non-empty).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v4","material_fingerprint":"9f84f2f023800d43","metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":1375134,"cache_write_tokens":328094,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":606.7,"input_tokens":1722805,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":193518.4,"output_tok